# World ↛ player

**The board does not require a controlled creature.** `World` + `GameSession.occupied` stand alone. Player input is optional via `ControlledCell` / `TurnManager.Controlled`. Personality focus (`CreatureTurnContext.Player`) is nullable.

## Hard rules

1. **Unified occupied.** Every living body (including the slime when present) is in `occupied`. No `PlayerCell` hole outside the set.
2. **No PlayerCell hard-blocks in Moves/Hunt.** Forbidden: `to != PlayerCell`, `cell == session.PlayerCell` as a special terrain rule.
3. **Controlled is optional.** `SetControlled(null)` / `Bind(world, controlled: null, …)` / `TakeTurn(..., player: null)` are valid.
4. **Hunt sims must not fake a slime.** Forbidden: inflate the map to 20×20 and park slime at `(19,19)` so Aggressive never sees it. Prefer board-only + `player: null`.
5. **Null player → Idle/Wander → hunt.** Do not add `if (!HasPlayer)` inside Combat; let Behavior conditions fail and Redirect own mob↔mob.

## Examples

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — mandatory player cell outside occupied; Moves special-cases PlayerCell
public GameSession(World world, Vector2Int playerCell, IEnumerable<Vector2Int> occupants)
{
    PlayerCell = playerCell; // not in occupied
}
if (to != session.PlayerCell && !session.IsOccupied(to)) { ... }
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — all bodies in occupied; controlled optional
var session = new GameSession(world, allCells);
session.SetControlled(slime?.Cell);
```

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — hunt test pads the map to hide a slime from Aggressive vision
var world = World.CreateGrass(20);
var player = Spawn<Slime>(new Vector2Int(19, 19));
dog.TakeTurn(session, player, rng, others);
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — board-only hunt
var world = World.CreateGrass(10);
var session = SessionFactory.Board(world, dog, cat);
dog.TakeTurn(session, player: null, rng, others);
```
